# No database refresh during tests

Tests use the shared MySQL database configured in `phpunit.xml`. **Never refresh, wipe, or re-migrate that database while tests run.**

## Forbidden

- `RefreshDatabase`, `LazilyRefreshDatabase`, or `DatabaseMigrations` traits
- `migrate:fresh`, `migrate:refresh`, `db:wipe`, or equivalent Artisan calls in tests
- `Schema::drop*` / rebuilding tables in test setup

## Required instead

- Use model factories to create only the records each test needs
- Prefer unique names/values (e.g. `fake()->unique()->word()`) when collisions matter
- Clean up only records the test created when necessary (delete specific models), not the whole schema
- Rely on existing schema; run migrations manually outside the test suite when the schema changes

## Example

```php
// ❌ BAD
uses(RefreshDatabase::class);

// ✅ GOOD
$user = User::factory()->create();
```
